<header><p class="st-kicker">theocracy · Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><h1 class="st-title">Marabout state of al-Ayyashi</h1><p class="st-meta">1614 CE – 1641 CE (approx.) · capital Salé</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The holy-war state of the marabout Muhammad al-Ayyashi, who led Moroccan resistance to Spanish coastal forts from Salé.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/larache">Larache</a> in 1610 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mehdya">La Mamora</a> in 1614 as the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/saadi-sultanate">Saadi Sultanate</a> fell apart. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-al-ayyashi">Muhammad al-Ayyashi</a>, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sufism">Sufi</a> disciple appointed as governor near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azemmour">Azemmour</a>, broke with the weak Saadi court and around 1614 began leading tribal holy war against the Christian forts, based at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sale">Salé</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-al-ayyashi">Al-Ayyashi</a>'s authority rested on religious charisma and the tribes of the Atlantic plains rather than formal institutions. He besieged <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mehdya">La Mamora</a> and Spanish and Portuguese positions, and controlled the region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sale">Salé</a>, clashing with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moriscos">Morisco</a> settlers of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/republic-of-sale">Republic of Salé</a>, whom he suspected of dealing with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1641 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-al-ayyashi">al-Ayyashi</a> was defeated and killed by forces allied with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/dilaiyya">Dila'iyya</a>, whose zawiya then took over his territory and influence over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sale">Salé</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="theocracy, 1614 CE – 1641 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M30 82 V46 Q50 12 70 46 V82 Z"/><path d="M50 30 V82 M40 58 H60"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">theocracy</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:91.82%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1614 CE – 1641 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>theocracy</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>theocratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Salé</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Muhammad al-Ayyashi</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam (Sufi)</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic, Berber</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/morocco">Morocco</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>al-Ayyashi, Mujahid state of Salé</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1628&amp;focus=marabout-state-of-al-ayyashi" aria-label="Marabout state of al-Ayyashi on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4506 944 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Marabout state of al-Ayyashi lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4826 1200L4873 1200"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4873 1200h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4826 1200h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4826 1200h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Salé. <a href="/atlas?year=1628&amp;focus=marabout-state-of-al-ayyashi">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
